  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="4ef0-552e-3bb3-62cf" name="Saxon (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>SAXON ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.34-35), the Anglo-Saxon fyrd and huscarls, 5th century to 1066.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Standard Bearer. Infantry at least half the points; Special Troops &amp; Mercenaries up to a quarter.
Huscarls: the army may include a single unit of Huscarls, either alone or split up and added to units of Fyrd. Huscarls must be placed in the front rank of the unit they are added to, never behind it. While at least half (rounding up) of the front rank are Huscarls the unit is not subject to Warband psychology, has Leadership 9 and is stubborn. Once the front rank has under 50% Huscarls the unit is subject to Warband psychology with Leadership 6 (Select Fyrd) or 5 (Fyrd). Half of all missile casualties on a combined Huscarl/Fyrd unit fall on Huscarl models. In hand-to-hand combat, enemy models in base contact with a Huscarl must fight against him.
Huscarl Hatred: if the army has a General and he is slain, Huscarls become subject to hatred for the rest of the battle, and so does any unit where Huscarls make up at least half the front rank.
Shield Wall: units of Huscarls and Fyrd spearmen may form a shield wall instead of moving; all enemy attacks from the front (shooting and hand-to-hand) suffer -1 to hit while the unit has not moved or lost a round of close combat.
Viking Mercenaries (not built here: make a separate small roster): the army may include Viking Huscarls from the Viking army list.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Special Troops &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
